# OpenCL Notes

## What I was trying to do
Understand how OpenCL kernels run on GPUs and CPUs.

## What I started with
- OpenCL 5.0 search results
- Intel OpenCL repos

## What each part does
- Platform: vendor backend
- Device: CPU/GPU/NPU
- Queue: where kernels run
- Buffers: memory objects

## What happened
- Kernel compilation is straightforward.
- Memory rules are strict.

## What confused me
- Different vendors behave differently.
- Extensions vary a lot.

## What I want to try next
- Write a simple kernel.
- Compare OpenCL vs oneAPI.

## Random thoughts
OpenCL feels like the “old but reliable” compute API.
